  "title": "Can a small push lift a bigger load? Hydraulic syringes #Shorts",
  "description": "Two connected syringes reveal Pascal’s principle. Ideal area ratio 4:1: 10 N produces 40 N, while 80 mm of input travel gives 20 mm at the larger piston. Work remains 0.8 J. Quasi-static, air-free incompressible-fluid model; friction, leakage, piston weight and hydrostatic head differences are omitted. This is a calculated kinematic visualization, not a CFD simulation. Cutaway barrels; flow cues are schematic.\n\nMusic:\nMonkeys Spinning Monkeys — Kevin MacLeod (incompetech.com)\nLicensed under Creative Commons Attribution 3.0\nhttps://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/3.0/\nMusic excerpt trimmed, faded and mixed beneath narration.\n\n\nPhysics reference: OpenStax, College Physics, Pascal’s Principle.\nhttps://github.com/openstax/osbooks-college-physics-bundle/blob/main/modules/m42193/index.cnxml",
